## 2026-09-23 — Checkpoint 03D ONNX preflight compatibility incident

The first workstation `python tools\\run_checkpoint_03d.py --preflight`
stopped before expensive training while converting the tiny ExtraTrees smoke
model. Stable `skl2onnx 1.20.0` passed boolean
`nodes_missing_value_tracks_true` values into ONNX 1.22+, which now requires
integer 0/1 attributes. Upstream fixed this after the 1.20.0 release.

Repository recovery:

- deployment extra pins `skl2onnx==1.20.0` and `onnx<1.22`;
- preflight prints exact deployment package versions;
- converter smoke tests are reported per model family;
- PLS may remain scientifically valid but be deployment-ineligible when its
  converter declares a non-single-target output schema;
- converter support no longer changes scientific finalist ranking;
- final ONNX export uses the highest-ranked finalist that passes schema and
  numerical equivalence checks;
- CatBoost uses its native ONNX exporter;
- XGBoost/LightGBM cap the requested opset to the maximum supported by
  `onnxmltools` rather than failing when config requests a newer opset;
- preflight now requires at least one verified nonlinear ONNX family, so a
  Ridge-only deployment path is no longer enough to declare readiness.

Workstation recovery command:

```powershell
git pull
conda activate geocebada
python -m pip install -e ".[dev,models,deployment]"
python tools\\run_checkpoint_03d.py --preflight
```

Do not start the long 03D run until this preflight passes.

