## Checkpoint 04B completed findings

Canonical interpretation: `docs/CHECKPOINT_04B_FINDINGS.md`. Generated evidence:
`reports/checkpoint_04b/`.

Key results:

```text
target-matched LocalRidge k20 alpha100       RMSE 0.4946
target-matched Graph k8 lambda2              RMSE 0.4974
target-matched LocalRidge k30 alpha100       RMSE 0.4976
target-matched GeoKNN k10                    RMSE 0.5021
target-matched GlobalPLS C0 4                RMSE 0.5379

Graph k8 lambda2:
  state-random                               RMSE 0.4655
  frozen state-stratified                    RMSE 0.4779
  frozen municipality-grouped               RMSE 0.5466
  worst-family                               RMSE 0.5466
```

LocalRidge k20 and Graph k8 are effectively near-tied on the 16 primary splits; LocalRidge wins
11/16 but only by mean RMSE 0.0028. Graph k8 is substantially more robust under the
municipality-grouped stress protocol.

Target-matched masks are meaningfully closer to the real 59-target X geometry than state-random
masks (municipality TV 0.0547 vs 0.0889; profile distance 0.5369 vs 0.9227).

The 04B support-tier routing proposal is exploratory only. It selected tier winners on the same
pseudo-test evidence used to compare methods and therefore needs leave-one-split-out or nested
validation before final routing. The X-only support score is also not a monotone uncertainty
measure: mid-support pseudo-targets were harder than low-support pseudo-targets.

Next priority:
1. tune graph topology/k/lambda and local Ridge neighborhood/regularization;
2. test residual graph correction on top of a global anchor;
3. validate any routing/gating rule out of sample;
4. run a focused high-compute CatBoost global anchor;
5. test SIAP 2025 municipality-level evidence as a local prior/node feature.


## Checkpoint 04D.1 implementation status

The local/graph refinement runner is committed:

```text
configs/checkpoint04d1.yaml
src/geocebada/evaluation/checkpoint04d1.py
src/geocebada/visualization/checkpoint04d1.py
tools/run_checkpoint_04d1.py
tests/test_checkpoint04d1.py
reports/checkpoint_04d1/README.md
```

The exhaustive primary grid contains 626 predefined methods:

```text
300 graph variants:
  5 distance topologies
  x 5 graph k values
  x 6 Laplacian regularization values
  x {direct y, cross-fitted-PLS-residual correction}

324 local Ridge variants:
  2 X representations (C1/C4)
  x 3 neighborhood distance topologies
  x 6 neighborhood sizes
  x 3 Ridge alphas
  x 3 inverse-distance powers

2 fixed anchors:
  GeoKNN10
  PLS4
```

Only the 16 target-matched splits receive the exhaustive search. The runner then performs
leave-one-split-out hyperparameter selection over that grid, selects three finalists per
graph/local family plus fixed anchors, and evaluates only those finalists on the 18 non-primary
stress splits.

Residual graph correction is leakage-safe with respect to pseudo-target y: the global PLS
anchor is fitted on visible labels, and the residual signal supplied to the graph is generated
by cross-fitting within the visible pseudo-training labels.

The actual 59 receive finalist candidate predictions only after validation. They are not the
final 04F output.


## Checkpoint 04D.1 completed findings

Canonical interpretation: `docs/CHECKPOINT_04D1_FINDINGS.md`. Generated evidence:
`reports/checkpoint_04d1/`.

```text
best target-matched Local Ridge C4 Geo k24 a30 p1  0.48785
LOSO model selection                               0.48837
LOSO support-tier routing                          0.48581
GraphDirect GeoAgro25 k6 lambda8 target-matched    0.49488
GraphDirect GeoAgro25 k6 lambda8 grouped stress    0.52788
```

The local optimum is stable across nearby configurations. The direct graph remains
the strongest robustness hedge when municipality-local labels are withheld. PLS
residual graph correction did not improve the direct graph.

## Checkpoint 04E.1 implementation status

04E.1 is implemented and run-pending. It adds a detailed SIAP loader that preserves
`Nomcicloproductivo` and `Nommodalidad`, then evaluates the following public
external-prior uses under the frozen 04B validation contract:

```text
SIAP direct municipal prior
visible-label affine calibration
SIAP + local Ridge residual correction
SIAP + graph residual correction
fixed blends with the 04D.1 local/graph survivors
```

The primary SIAP scope is exactly `Cebada grano + Primavera-Verano + Temporal +
CVEGEO + 2025`. Broader grain-barley scopes are explicit named fallbacks only.
No hidden parcel yield is accessed.


## 2026-09-23 — Checkpoint 03D runtime reduction

The initial 03D full grid was too expensive for 138 labeled parcels: CatBoost outer
fits were taking about 15 minutes each because every outer fold contained a
9-candidate x 3-inner-fold search plus refit. The default 03D config is now a
balanced-compute benchmark:

- preserve both frozen 5-fold outer protocols;
- preserve 3-fold inner CV;
- use 3 representative candidates for CatBoost, XGBoost, LightGBM, ExtraTrees,
  and HistGB instead of the wider 6-9 candidate grids;
- cap boosted models at 2500 estimators/iterations;
- reduce ExtraTrees from 3000 to 1500 trees.

This reduces inner/refit count from roughly 5570 fits to roughly 2540 before
accounting for shorter individual fits. The statistical evaluation structure is
unchanged; the reduction is in redundant hyperparameter tuning.

Important: partial results from the former wide grid must NOT be resumed into the
balanced grid. The runner now fingerprints the config/model/representation/compute
selection in _partial_state.json. A mismatch aborts --resume. Starting once
without --resume clears stale partials; subsequent interruptions can safely use
--resume.


## 2026-09-24 — Checkpoint 03D completed

Balanced 03D completed in 248.085 minutes with 230 outer fits and 6,348 OOF
rows across 23 eligible pairs. The robust finalists were all G1 agronomic:
HistGBLarge (state/grouped 0.549924/0.715339), XGBoostLarge
(0.525847/0.733080) and LightGBMLarge (0.540812/0.748478).

The result improves grouped global robustness relative to the frozen 03C
frontier but does not dominate both protocols. Broad global tuning is closed.

HistGB rank 1 was not ONNX-convertible under the stable stack. XGBoost rank 2
was the highest-ranked deployable finalist and its ONNX round trip passed with
maximum absolute difference 3.814697e-06. The global ONNX artifact is not
Local04D.

Do not compare state/grouped 03D RMSE directly with Local04D's target-matched
0.487845 as though they came from the same validation protocol.


## 2026-10-03 — Checkpoint 06 tail/regime plan opened

A teammate reported a possible residual pattern: Local04D and CatBoost appear to
predict most parcels well but miss a small number of very low- and high-yield
parcels. Because RMSE squares errors, a small extreme subset could dominate the
remaining objective.

This is not yet established. Checkpoint 06 was opened specifically to test the
claim before modeling it.

Canonical plan: `docs/CHECKPOINT_06_PLAN.md`.

The plan requires tail/SSE diagnostics, fold-valid tail definitions,
Local-vs-CatBoost error-overlap analysis, feature-family/variable importance,
tail/error-risk prediction from X, low-capacity calibration, conditional X-only
clustering and partially pooled regime correction. Promotion requires target-
matched development, LOSO and a new fresh confirmation bank.

No 06 model/result exists yet and no final prediction changed.
